SUMMARY:Panigiri of Pera Panagia\, Panagia village
LOCATION:Panagia\, Kasos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The biggest day of the Kasos year: the whole island\, plus 2\,000-odd diaspora Kasiots\, gathers at the church in the village of Panagia. Kasiot dolmadakia (tiny stuffed vine leaves)\, stewed meat with cinnamon pilaf and fried potatoes are served free\, and sousta and zervos dancing to lyra and laouto runs from midday to dawn. Ferries and the tiny plane fill up\; book in June.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#panagia-panigiri-of-pera-panagia-panagia-village
